Most of the doc changes follow one consistent pattern. Defaults move into `<value>`, and behavioral notes move into `<remarks>`. `<see langword="null"/>` and `<see langword="false"/>` replace bare words, and `<code language="csharp">` is used on the example block. This makes the rendered API docs easier to scan and matches the output of the .NET API docs tooling.

::callout{type="info"}
The `TryGetValidatableTypeInfo` change that moves `validatableTypeInfo = null;` to the top of the method is behavior-neutral, because the out parameter is always assigned before the loop returns. The new placement is also clearer.
